  "rulings": [
    {
      "comment": "Galadhrim Ambush counts all attacking creatures no matter which player, planeswalker, or battle they're attacking, including attacking creatures you control if Galadhrim Ambush is cast during your combat phase.",
      "oracle_id": "3b22d21f-e19a-40df-840b-a2b7f11f79c2",
      "published_at": "2023-06-16",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Although Terrifying Presence doesn\u2019t affect the target creature, if that creature is an illegal target when Terrifying Presence tries to resolve, it won\u2019t resolve and none of its effects will happen. No damage will be prevented.",
      "oracle_id": "ca8f6e19-6ef3-4d77-8312-867767ffeda6",
      "published_at": "2012-05-01",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If there are fewer than twenty cards in the targeted player's library, that player puts all the cards from their library into their graveyard.",
      "oracle_id": "cc2b6e58-2d6f-495e-95f3-9496105c4cba",
      "published_at": "2009-10-01",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "This card now uses the Reach keyword ability to enable the blocking of flying creatures. This works because a creature with flying can only be blocked by creatures with flying or reach.",
      "oracle_id": "e740ce2f-2134-473c-afa1-1b6d2d1e38ef",
      "published_at": "2008-04-01",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If a card with flashback is put into your graveyard during your turn, you can cast it if it's legal to do so before any other player can take any actions.",
      "oracle_id": "a3ec6b5d-08ec-4ae0-b1db-c4b87a1849c7",
      "published_at": "2021-03-19",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "To determine the total cost of a spell, start with the mana cost or alternative cost (such as a flashback cost) you're paying, add any cost increases, then apply any cost reductions. The mana value of the spell is determined only by its mana cost, no matter what the total cost to cast the spell was.",
      "oracle_id": "a3ec6b5d-08ec-4ae0-b1db-c4b87a1849c7",
      "published_at": "2021-03-19",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "You can cast a spell using flashback even if it was somehow put into your graveyard without having been cast.",
      "oracle_id": "a3ec6b5d-08ec-4ae0-b1db-c4b87a1849c7",
      "published_at": "2021-03-19",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "\"Flashback [cost]\" means \"You may cast this card from your graveyard by paying [cost] rather than paying its mana cost\" and \"If the flashback cost was paid, exile this card instead of putting it anywhere else any time it would leave the stack.\"",
      "oracle_id": "a3ec6b5d-08ec-4ae0-b1db-c4b87a1849c7",
      "published_at": "2021-03-19",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A spell cast using flashback will always be exiled afterward, whether it resolves, is countered, or leaves the stack in some other way.",
      "oracle_id": "a3ec6b5d-08ec-4ae0-b1db-c4b87a1849c7",
      "published_at": "2021-03-19",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "You must still follow any timing restrictions and permissions, including those based on the card's type. For instance, you can cast a sorcery using flashback only when you could normally cast a sorcery.",
      "oracle_id": "a3ec6b5d-08ec-4ae0-b1db-c4b87a1849c7",
      "published_at": "2021-03-19",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "When the card returns to the battlefield, it will be a new object with no connection to the card that was exiled. Auras attached to the exiled creature will be put into their owners' graveyards. Any Equipment will become unattached and remain on the battlefield. Any counters on the exiled creature will cease to exist.",
      "oracle_id": "a3ec6b5d-08ec-4ae0-b1db-c4b87a1849c7",
      "published_at": "2022-12-08",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If a token is exiled this way, it will cease to exist and won't return to the battlefield.",
      "oracle_id": "a3ec6b5d-08ec-4ae0-b1db-c4b87a1849c7",
      "published_at": "2022-12-08",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If an attacking creature loses haste, perhaps because Fervor leaves the battlefield after attackers have been declared, it won't be removed from combat.",
      "oracle_id": "8e0cea9c-3110-4728-9378-76849e33bb90",
      "published_at": "2012-07-01",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If a spell or ability causes you to draw multiple cards, Thought Reflection's effect doubles each card draw. For example, if you cast Harmonize (\u201cDraw three cards\u201d), you'll draw six cards.",
      "oracle_id": "692a6833-3014-42f6-b1ad-333bb3292c65",
      "published_at": "2020-08-07",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If two or more replacement effects would apply to a card-drawing event, the player who's drawing the card chooses what order to apply them.",
      "oracle_id": "692a6833-3014-42f6-b1ad-333bb3292c65",
      "published_at": "2020-08-07",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The effects of multiple Thought Reflections are cumulative. For example, if you have two Thought Reflections on the battlefield, you'll draw four times the original number of cards. If you have three, you'll draw eight times the number of cards, and so on.",
      "oracle_id": "692a6833-3014-42f6-b1ad-333bb3292c65",
      "published_at": "2020-08-07",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The damage Questing Beast deals to the target planeswalker as its last ability resolves isn't combat damage.",
      "oracle_id": "b685757b-521e-4353-a233-97052359723d",
      "published_at": "2019-10-04",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Once a creature with power 3 or greater has blocked this creature, changing the power of the blocking creature won't cause this creature to become unblocked.",
      "oracle_id": "b685757b-521e-4353-a233-97052359723d",
      "published_at": "2019-10-04",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Questing Beast only stops combat damage from being prevented by effects that specifically use the word \u201cprevent.\u201d",
      "oracle_id": "b685757b-521e-4353-a233-97052359723d",
      "published_at": "2019-10-04",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If the opponent dealt damage controls no planeswalkers, Questing Beast's last ability simply does nothing.",
      "oracle_id": "b685757b-521e-4353-a233-97052359723d",
      "published_at": "2019-10-04",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "This spell only affects creatures on the battlefield when it resolves.",
      "oracle_id": "2d4e0e0f-7167-40a4-ad76-2d5b45223eaa",
      "published_at": "2004-10-04",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The creatures are counted on resolution.",
      "oracle_id": "70e0b676-61a2-4dcf-8f61-d9281467ed43",
      "published_at": "2004-10-04",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "In a Two-Headed Giant game, only Boon Reflection's controller is affected by it. If that player's teammate gains life, Boon Reflection will have no effect, even when that life gain is applied to the shared team life total.",
      "oracle_id": "b86d3142-568a-4eea-b1ae-5fcfc1453533",
      "published_at": "2020-08-07",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If an effect would set your life total to a specific number that's higher than your current life total, that effect would cause you to gain life equal to the difference. Boon Reflection will then double the amount of life that effect would cause you to gain. For example, if you have 3 life and an effect says that your life total \u201cbecomes 10,\u201d your life total will actually become 17.",
      "oracle_id": "b86d3142-568a-4eea-b1ae-5fcfc1453533",
      "published_at": "2020-08-07",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The effects of multiple Boon Reflections are cumulative. For example, if you control two Boon Reflections, you'll gain four times the original amount of life. If you control three Boon Reflections, you'll gain eight times the original amount, and so on.",
      "oracle_id": "b86d3142-568a-4eea-b1ae-5fcfc1453533",
      "published_at": "2020-08-07",
      "source": "wotc"
    }
  ],
